From 4e084ff8992342df9937865f0f73b3f388e885a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:03:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: the owner turns an undeliverable
 synced ask into a visible one

Review and adversarial pass of the previous head (reviewer APPROVE with this
as its Medium): a pool worker's chat wait skips the subscriber check (the
owner holds the subscriptions), so when the owner has no chat that can take
it the ask was recorded, synced and read by nobody.

- Sync apply records an imported decision_requested for a card this gateway
  owns (ApplyResult.decision_asks). After the commit, owner_fallback checks
  has_chat_subscriber; with none, the still-parked card leaves the park
  (scheduled -> triage, probe cleared, decision_unanswerable event, as the
  spend-budget hold does) and is blocked needs_input with a human_request
  carrying the question. If that block is refused it stays visible in triage.
- --skip-system also ignores the older kernel writers without the kanban-
  prefix (dispatcher, placement, worker-placement, triage-sweep, respawn-guard,
  quota/oom/dup detectors, gateway).

Tests: an imported ask on an owned card with no wakeable chat blocks it with
the question; with a wakeable chat it stays parked; dispatcher and placement
notes do not fire the probe. 3 of 49 fail on the previous head; 35 neighbour
files (638 tests) and 75 sync files (1837 tests) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
